8. Mental Models
8.1 Maze Exploration
DFS walks down a path until it cannot continue, then backs up and tries another
path.
8.2 Paint Bucket
Starting from one node, DFS spreads to all connected nodes and marks them.
This is useful for islands and connected components.
8.3 Call Stack as Path
Recursive DFS uses the call stack to remember where to return after finishing a
branch.
8.4 Visited Means Already Processed
Once a node is visited, do not process it again.
This prevents infinite loops and duplicate work.
