pdfNotes.coreIntuition:
Core Intuition
BFS works in waves.
Start from one or more sources.
Then expand to all neighbors.
Then expand to neighbors of neighbors.
Each layer represents one more step.
step 0: start
step 1: all nodes one edge away
step 2: all nodes two edges away
step 3: all nodes three edges away
The first time you reach the target, the step count is minimum.
8. Mental Models
8.1 Fire Spreading

Fire spreads from a starting cell to adjacent cells every minute.
This models Rotting Oranges.
8.2 Ripples in Water
A stone dropped in water creates expanding rings.
BFS expands like rings.
8.3 Queue of Frontiers
The queue stores nodes discovered but not processed yet.
FIFO order ensures closer nodes are processed before farther nodes.
8.4 First Visit Is Best Visit
In unweighted BFS:
first time reaching a node = shortest distance to that node
So mark visited when pushing into queue.
