pdfNotes.coreIntuition:
Core Intuition
Topological sort repeatedly processes nodes with no remaining prerequisites.
A node with no prerequisites has:
indegree = 0
Indegree means number of incoming edges.
If:
u -> v
then v has one prerequisite from u.
Once u is processed, we reduce vs indegree.
When vs indegree becomes 0, it is ready.

8. Mental Models
8.1 Course Prerequisites
You can take a course only after all prerequisites are done.
Courses with no prerequisites can be taken first.
8.2 Dependency Unlocking
Completing one task unlocks dependent tasks.
8.3 Peeling Layers
Topological sort peels off nodes with indegree 0 layer by layer.
8.4 Cycle Trap
If no node has indegree 0 but nodes remain, those nodes are trapped in a cycle.
9. Pattern Recognition Checklist
Ask:
17.
Are there directed dependencies?
18.
Does one item need to come before another?
19.
Does the problem ask if all tasks can be completed?
20.
Does the problem ask for an order?
21.
Does a cycle make completion impossible?
22.
Can I model prerequisite as an edge?
23.
Do I need process nodes with no prerequisites first?
24.
Does indegree make sense?
25.
Is this a DAG problem?
26.
Is the graph directed?
If yes, topological sort may apply.
