8. Optimization 1  Simple Space
Optimization
8.1 Idea
If a DP state only depends on the previous one or two states, do not store the full array.
Example:
Fibonacci:
dp[i] = dp[i - 1] + dp[i - 2]
Only need:
prev2
prev1
8.2 Example  Fibonacci
class Solution {
public:
    int fib(int n) {
        if (n <= 1) {
            return n;
        }

        int prev2 = 0;
        int prev1 = 1;

        for (int i = 2; i <= n; i++) {
            int curr = prev1 + prev2;
            prev2 = prev1;
            prev1 = curr;
        }

        return prev1;
    }
};
8.3 Complexity
Before:
Time: O(n)
Space: O(n)
After:
Time: O(n)
Space: O(1)

9. Optimization 2  Rolling Array for
Grid DP
9.1 Idea
If:
dp[r][c]
depends only on:
previous row
current row left cell
then one row is enough.
9.2 Example  Unique Paths
2D recurrence:
dp[r][c] = dp[r - 1][c] + dp[r][c - 1]
Space optimized:
class Solution {
public:
    int uniquePaths(int m, int n) {
        vector<int> dp(n, 1);

        for (int r = 1; r < m; r++) {
            for (int c = 1; c < n; c++) {
                dp[c] += dp[c - 1];
            }
        }

        return dp[n - 1];
    }
};
9.3 Why This Works

At cell c:
dp[c]     before update = value from previous row
dp[c - 1] after update  = value from current row left cell
So:
dp[c] = dp[c] + dp[c - 1];
means:
top + left

